{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), giving us a weak baseline with high uncertainty about every design axis. The largest open question is whether the image modality contributes meaningful signal at all, since it fundamentally determines whether we should invest remaining budget in multimodal configurations or focus on RNA encoder/profile variations. This experiment (config_016: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal extension of config_001—it keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting and only adds the image branch with the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of adding image modality. If it substantially beats 48.5%, we gain strong evidence to exploit multimodal configurations in later experiments; if it does not, we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder and profile-setting comparisons. With 8 experiments remaining, resolving the modality question early is the highest-value use of the next slot."
}

